nta, Georgia."}]}}, {"fullName": "Bremer E", "lastName": "Bremer", "firstName": "Erich", "initials": "E", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0223-1059"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Informatics, Stony Brook Medicine, Stony Brook, New York."}]}}, {"fullName": "Almeida JS", "lastName": "Almeida", "firstName": "Jonas S", "initials": "JS", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics, National Cancer Institute, National Institutes of Health, Bethesda, Maryland."}]}}, {"fullName": "Saltz J", "lastName": "Saltz", "firstName": "Joel", "initials": "J", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Informatics, Stony Brook Medicine, Stony Brook, New York."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6214-1923"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3715-7699"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-9513-4620"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0223-1059"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2723-5902"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "7", "volume": "190", "journalIssueId": 2970274, "dateOfPublication": "2020 Jul", "monthOfPublication": 7, "yearOfPublication": 2020, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Am J Pathol", "title": "The American journal of pathology", "essn": "1525-2191", "issn": "0002-9440", "nlmid": "0370502", "isoabbreviation": "Am J Pathol"}, "printPublicationDate": "2020-07-01"}, "pubYear": "2020", "pageInfo": "1491-1504", "abstractText": "Quantitative assessment of spatial relations between tumor and tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes (TIL) is increasingly important in both basic science and clinical aspects of breast cancer research. We have developed and evaluated convolutional neural network analysis pipelines to generate combined maps of cancer regions and TILs in routine diagnostic breast cancer whole slide tissue images. The combined maps provide insight about the structural patterns and spatial distribution of lymphocytic infiltrates and facilitate improved quantification of TILs. Both tumor and TIL analyses were evaluated by using three convolutional neural network networks (34-layer ResNet, 16-layer VGG, and Inception v4); the results compared favorably with those obtained by using the best published methods. We have produced open-source tools and a public data set consisting of tumor/TIL maps for 1090 invasive breast cancer images from The Cancer Genome Atlas. The maps can be downloaded for further downstream analyses.", "affiliation": "Department of Computer Science, Stony Brook University, Stony Brook, New York. Electronic address: hdle@cs.stonybrook.edu.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "National Cancer Institute", "grantId": "1UG3CA225021-01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NLM NIH HHS", "acronym": "LM", "grantId": "R01 LM011119", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U24 CA215109", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "UG3 CA225021", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Science Foundation", "grantId": "ACI-1445606", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "U.S. National Library of Medicine", "grantId": "R01LM011119-01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIGMS NIH HHS", "acronym": "GM", "grantId": "T32 GM008444", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U24 CA180924", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Cancer Institute", "grantId": "3U24CA215109-02", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Science Foundation", "grantId": "ACI-1548562", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NLM NIH HHS", "acronym":